:"It depends on what matters most. St Kitts & Nevis is the strongest and fastest, Dominica is the most affordable, Antigua suits large families, and Grenada is the only one with a route to the US E-2 visa."},{"cat":"Family","home":true,"q":"Can I include my family?","a":"Yes. Every programme lets you add your spouse and dependent children, and most allow dependent parents. Some also allow siblings. Age limits differ by country."},{"cat":"Family","home":false,"q":"Will my future children be citizens too?","a":"Yes. Citizenship passes by descent, so children born after you become a citizen can apply as well."},{"cat":"Costs","home":false,"q":"How much does it cost in total?","a":"Programmes start at $200,000 for a single applicant. On top of the investment there are government processing, due-diligence and passport fees, plus our professional fee. We give you one written quote before you commit."},{"cat":"Costs","home":false,"q":"When do I pay the investment?","a":"Only after the government has approved your application in principle. You pay the government or approved developer directly, never through us."},{"cat":"Costs","home":false,"q":"Do I get my money back?","a":"Fund contributions are non-refundable. Real estate is an asset you own and can sell after the required holding period. Saint Lucia’s bond option is returned after the holding period."},{"cat":"Process","home":true,"q":"How long does it take?","a":"Typically 4 to 9 months from submission. St Kitts & Nevis is usually fastest. Preparing documents adds 2 to 6 weeks at the start."},{"cat":"Process","home":true,"q":"Do I need to travel or attend an interview?","a":"No interview or language test is required, and the whole application can be done from wherever you live. Antigua & Barbuda asks for a 5-day visit within the first five years."},{"cat":"Process","home":false,"q":"What could get my application refused?","a":"Usually a criminal record, a previous visa refusal that wasn’t disclosed, or funds whose source can’t be proven. We review your profile at the start so there are no surprises."},{"cat":"Living & travel","home":false,"q":"Do I have to live in the country?","a":"No. Apart from Antigua’s short visit, there is no residency requirement. You can keep living and working where you are."},{"cat":"Living & travel","home":false,"q":"Which countries can I visit visa-free?","a":"Between about 145 and 155 destinations depending on the passport, including the Schengen area and Singapore. The exact list differs by country, so ask us for the one you’re considering."},{"cat":"Living & travel","home":false,"q":"Will I pay tax there?","a":"The Caribbean CBI countries do not tax the worldwide income of non-residents. Your tax position at home and elsewhere depends on your own circumstances, so take independent advice."}]}